## Context

Before fully trusting the mart flow, run old and new analysis paths side by
side and gate cutover on parity thresholds.

## Parity scope

Parity is checked on **CSV intermediates, not rendered PDFs**. PDFs are not
bit-reproducible (font embedding, timestamps). The parity contract is:

- Tables (`tab_*.csv`): exact column-set and row-count match; numeric fields
  within ±0.001 relative tolerance (floating-point formatting may differ).
- Figure inputs (`*_view.csv` consumed by plot scripts): same exact/tolerance
  policy as tables.
- Rendered PDFs: excluded from parity — visual inspection only.

## Deliverables

1. Dual-run Makefile targets: `make exp2-old-path` and `make exp2-mart-path`
   producing outputs into separate staging directories
2. Parity checker comparing the CSV intermediates listed above
3. CI/local gate target `make check-mart-parity` failing on regressions
4. Documented tolerance policy (in the gate script or its docstring)

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `make exp2-old-path` and `make exp2-mart-path` targets exist
- [ ] `make check-mart-parity` checks CSV intermediates with documented tolerances
- [ ] Parity checks pass on current baseline
- [ ] Rendered PDFs are explicitly excluded from automated parity
- [ ] `make check-fast` passes
